From: ArchivalEra <archivalera@localhost>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v2] irqchip/gic: hi3798mv310: dump banked SGI/PPI state,
 keep Group 1 enables except GICD_CTLR bit 1

v2: the GICD_CTLR bit 1 (EnableGrp1) write is retracted.  Board bisect
(2026-08-19, mv310, GIC-400): the only runtime difference between a
booting image (GICD_CTLR=0x1, devmem baseline) and a hanging image
(GICD_CTLR=0x3) is that bit.  The 0x3 image hangs in time_init()
immediately after the sched_clock line, with no further serial output.
The non-secure view of mv310's GICD_CTLR accepts bit 1 (unlike
standard GIC-400 NS banking where bit 0 is the EnableGrp1NS alias) and
enabling it wedges the boot.  The write is dropped; GICD_CTLR stays at
the known-good 0x1.

What remains in this patch:

 - gic_cpu_if_up(): also set GICC_CTLR.EnableGrp1 (bit 1).  Validated
   on the grp1fix image (log gicc_ctlr=0x3e3); does not change boot.
 - gic_dist_init(): write GICD_IGROUPR0 = 0xffffffff (SGIs/PPIs ->
   Group 1).  Harmless on GIC-400, the relevant bits already read 1.
 - gic_cpu_init(): one-shot per-CPU dump of the banked SGI/PPI state
   (GICD_CTLR/TYPER/IGROUPR0/ISENABLER0/ICFGR1/GICC_CTLR/GICC_PMR)
   with register offsets spelled out in the message itself, so the
   next serial log cannot be misread the way "ISENABLER0 == 0" was
   (that read was at 0xf1001104 = GICD_ISENABLER1, SPI 32-63; the
   real ISENABLER0 is at 0xf1001100 and is 0xffff at runtime).
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-gic.c | 66 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 65 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic.c
@@ -457,7 +457,13 @@
 	bypass = readl(cpu_base + GIC_CPU_CTRL);
 	bypass &= GICC_DIS_BYPASS_MASK;
 
-	writel_relaxed(bypass | mode | GICC_ENABLE, cpu_base + GIC_CPU_CTRL);
+	/*
+	 * hi3798mv310: also set GICC_CTLR.EnableGrp1 (bit 1). This was
+	 * validated on the grp1fix image (log: gicc_ctlr=0x3e3) and does
+	 * not change boot behavior.
+	 */
+	writel_relaxed(bypass | mode | GICC_ENABLE |
+		       GIC_CPU_CTRL_EnableGrp1, cpu_base + GIC_CPU_CTRL);
 }
 
 
@@ -481,6 +487,23 @@
 
 	gic_dist_config(base, gic_irqs, GICD_INT_DEF_PRI);
 
+	/*
+	 * hi3798mv310: force SGI/PPI (INTID 0-31) into Group 1 in the
+	 * non-secure banked view.  Harmless on GIC-400 (the relevant bits
+	 * already read 1 on this board).
+	 */
+	writel_relaxed(0xffffffff, base + GIC_DIST_IGROUP);
+
+	/*
+	 * NOTE: do NOT write GICD_CTLR bit 1 (EnableGrp1) from the kernel
+	 * on this board.  Bisect (2026-08-19): the only runtime difference
+	 * between a booting and a hanging image is GICD_CTLR 0x1 -> 0x3,
+	 * and the 0x3 image hangs in time_init() right after sched_clock.
+	 * The non-secure view of mv310's GICD_CTLR accepts bit 1 (non
+	 * standard for GIC-400 NS banking, where bit 0 is the EnableGrp1NS
+	 * alias) and enabling it wedges the boot.  Keep the plain
+	 * GICD_ENABLE write (0x1) which is the known-good value.
+	 */
 	writel_relaxed(GICD_ENABLE, base + GIC_DIST_CTRL);
 }
 
@@ -521,6 +544,23 @@
 	writel_relaxed(GICC_INT_PRI_THRESHOLD, base + GIC_CPU_PRIMASK);
 	gic_cpu_if_up(gic);
 
+	/*
+	 * hi3798mv310 bring-up aid: dump the banked SGI/PPI state exactly
+	 * as this CPU's non-secure view sees it, with offsets spelled out
+	 * so a serial log cannot be misread again.  Note the trap that
+	 * cost a full investigation day: GICD_ISENABLER0 is at dist+0x100
+	 * (0xf1001100); 0xf1001104 is GICD_ISENABLER1 (SPI 32-63).
+	 */
+	pr_info("MV310-GIC[%u]: GICD_CTLR(+0x000)=0x%08x GICD_TYPER(+0x004)=0x%08x IGROUPR0(+0x080)=0x%08x ISENABLER0(+0x100)=0x%08x ICFGR1(+0xc04)=0x%08x GICC_CTLR(+0x000)=0x%08x GICC_PMR(+0x004)=0x%08x\n",
+		cpu,
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + GIC_DIST_CTRL),
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + 0x004),
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + GIC_DIST_IGROUP),
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + GIC_DIST_ENABLE_SET),
+		readl_relaxed(dist_base + GIC_DIST_CONFIG + 0x4),
+		readl_relaxed(base + GIC_CPU_CTRL),
+		readl_relaxed(base + GIC_CPU_PRIMASK));
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
